    sampleAnswer: "Name filtering can use WHERE, LIKE, or other string predicates, while GROUP BY aggregates rows into groups.\n\n    SELECT department, COUNT(*) AS employee_count\n    FROM employees\n    WHERE name LIKE 'A%'\n    GROUP BY department;\n\nThe key distinction is that WHERE filters rows before grouping, while HAVING filters groups after aggregation.",
